WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.970
At the very centre of
a great painted wheel,

2
00:00:03.020 --> 00:00:05.040
three animals circle.

3
00:00:05.090 --> 00:00:06.000
A pig.

4
00:00:06.050 --> 00:00:07.110
A rooster.

5
00:00:07.160 --> 00:00:08.430
A snake.

6
00:00:08.480 --> 00:00:13.640
Each one bites the tail of the
next, round and round, without end.

7
00:00:13.690 --> 00:00:17.360
Buddhist artists paint them at
the heart of the Wheel of Life.

8
00:00:17.410 --> 00:00:20.370
So what are these three
animals doing to us?

9
00:00:20.420 --> 00:00:24.400
In this mission, you'll hear what the
Buddha named as the cause of suffering in

10
00:00:24.450 --> 00:00:26.170
his first sermon.

11
00:00:26.220 --> 00:00:31.060
Then you'll meet three kinds of craving,
and test them on everyday wishes.

12
00:00:31.110 --> 00:00:36.000
Your mission: find out what the pig,
the rooster and the snake stand for,

13
00:00:36.050 --> 00:00:36.990
and what they do.
